      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
      ":question/worked-solution": "The period of $y=\\tan x$ is $\\pi .$ Therefore, for integer $n$ we have\n\n$$\n\\tan x=\\tan (x+n\\pi ).\n$$\n\nSubstituting $n=1$ into the right-hand-side of the above gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\tan x=\\tan (x+1\\cdot \\pi )=\\tan (x+1\\pi ).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, if $\\tan x=-16,$ we get that $\\tan (x+1\\pi )=-16.$"
    },
