      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/hard",
      ":question/worked-solution": "The period of $y=\\tan x$ is $\\pi .$ Therefore, for any integer $n,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\tan x=\\tan (x+n\\pi ).\n$$\n\nSubstituting $n=1$ into the above gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\tan x=\\tan (x+1\\cdot \\pi )=\\tan (x+1\\pi ).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $\\tan x=-\\frac{1}{2},$ we get that $\\tan (x+1\\pi )=-\\frac{1}{2}.$ Therefore\n\n$$\n\\left(-\\frac{1}{2}\\right)\\tan (x+1\\pi )-1=-\\frac{1}{2}(-\\frac{1}{2})-1=\\frac{1}{4}-1=-\\frac{3}{4}.\n$$"
